## Key Findings

* Frances Tiafoe and Learner Tien lead the overall results with win rates near 68%, followed closely by Taylor Fritz and Tommy Paul.
* Learner Tien has combined strong overall performance with a 75% hard-court win rate and excellent deciding-set and tiebreak results.
* Taylor Fritz has the strongest qualifying grass-court record at 80%, while Ben Shelton leads on hard courts at 73%.
* Ben Shelton recorded six wins at the Canada Masters, the highest total by one player at a single tournament. Taylor Fritz earned four wins at Wimbledon.
* Zachary Svajda leads with six victories over higher-ranked opponents. Alex Michelsen, Ethan Quinn, Learner Tien, and Michael Zheng each have four.
* Results became more stable as the season progressed, with the leading Americans maintaining cumulative win rates of approximately 60%–70%.

*Results reflect the available 2026 data. Percentages based on smaller match samples should be interpreted cautiously.*
